  "limitations": [
    "DEL-04 still owns Alembic migration files, catalog relational tables and foreign keys, and production bootstrap that migrates then calls the insert-only configuration seed before serving. API-03 proves durability and reseed behavior against tables created from current ORM metadata but does not claim a deployed migration.",
    "API-09 still owns the unified application/problem+json vocabulary, Origin validation, process-local CSRF token/session contract, and global timeout policy. API-03 requires JSON, a server-issued human local_admin, and a strong If-Match validator but is not yet claimed browser-CSRF-safe.",
    "Ingress, planner, run snapshot, and scheduler consumption of revised configuration remain with API-04, API-05, ORCH-01, RUN-02, SCHED-01, and related later requirements. Updating schedule configuration does not yet materialize or mutate a scheduler row.",
    "Only deterministic local mock connector binding IDs are registered in this requirement. Real connector registration and encrypted secret references remain later adapter and deployment scope; secret values are never accepted as configuration fields.",
    "WEB-03 and DEL-07 still own configuration UI controls, the committed OpenAPI snapshot, generated client, and drift gate. PostgreSQL DDL remains portable, but the optional PostgreSQL runtime driver may be skipped locally and no live PostgreSQL server is exercised."
